	(text "The INA301A1 gain is 20 V/V. Each LIMIT pin uses 10 kOhm to GND;\nRESET is grounded for transparent alerts. The four open-drain ALERT\noutputs join OC_OK_N. An overcurrent pulls this shared line low,\nindependently of ADC sampling; fault memory is in the power-control logic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 91.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c6f49dea-35fd-4f70-9f0f-2a057bba5ab8")
	)
	(text "This sheet supervises DDR1V35, PHY1V05, ANA5 and ANA3V3. These rails\nsupport MIRA's memory, Ethernet link and analog conversion circuits.\nLoad-side voltage and current telemetry lets the power manager verify\nstartup and diagnose faults in the digital and low-noise analog branches."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 45.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c971fd30-3209-4b93-81a2-a90ebd39f26d")
	)
